<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Patta Chundawat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1568">1568</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Fatta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Patta, also known as Fatta, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sisodia">Sisodia</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> chief of Kelwa in Mewar who with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaimal-rathore">Jaimal Rathore</a> led the defence of Chittor against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a>'s siege of 1567–1568. He was killed in the final assault in February 1568. Together with Jaimal he became a hero of Rajput tradition, and Akbar honoured the two defenders with statues at the gate of the fort at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agra">Agra</a>.</p></div>
